there's no point messing around with hacks and kludges when there are legit
mechanisms in place.  Indeed, you can even argue that "I wasn't posting NEWS,
I was sending E-MAIL", this way.  I'd bet that's a "Get out of jail free card"
good for one offense.  If you want to go a middle course, you can always post
anonymously, but include your E-mail address at the end.  That way you could
keep "plausible deniability" for one offense.  If they're monitoring your
outgoing E-mail though, you really have only one option:  PGP encrypt your
message and send it to a cypherpunk remailer, which then reposts to whatever
newsgroup.  See alt.anonymous, alt.security.pgp, comp.security.pgp, for details
   Meanwhile, to all those enlightened souls who would let a state-supported
