But, ...
Canadian Army Private Elvin Kyle Brown was convicted of torture
and manslaughter in the death of the Somali prisoner.  During his trial,
and up until just a few days ago, Canadians were NOT ALLOWED TO KNOW
that the real killer was Master Corporal Clayton Matchee.

Because of the publication ban, when the Canadian magazine Maclean's (March 28)
did a recent "expose'" and "blow-by-blow" account of the tragic death
in Somalia, Private Brown was on the cover, and despite an apparently
detailed and "factual" account, Master Corporal Matchee was never mentioned.
