Possible policy:

   "As an upper limit, do not post (or cross post) an article (or set
    of very similar articles) in any 24-hour period to more than the
    square root of the number of newsgroups (rounded up) that this
    site receives.

    We currently subscribe to 3002 newsgroups, so you shouldn't post
    any article to any more than 55 newsgroups. Although it is not a
    violation of this upper limit, posting to even 55 (or even 5)
    newsgroups is a lot and is discouraged."

Good parts of such a policy:

    Using a mechanical definition of "very similar", this policy could
    be enforced automatically.

    The use of square root is inspired by a theorem from the field of
    computational learning theory. It says that (under certain)
    circumstances) sublinear compression without information loss
    implies generalization/learning/prediction.

